/**
 * Master mode selection 2 
 *
 *   0x0  Reset - the UG bit from the TIMx_EGR register is used as trigger output (tim_trgo2).
 *   0x1  Enable - the Counter Enable signal CNT_EN is used as trigger output (tim_trgo2).
 *   0x2  Update - the update event is selected as trigger output (tim_trgo2).
 *   0x3  Compare pulse - the trigger output sends a positive pulse when the CC1IF flag is to be set (even if it was already high), as soon as a capture or compare match occurs (tim_trgo2).
 *   0x4  Compare - tim_oc1refc signal is used as trigger output (tim_trgo2)
 *   0x5  Compare - tim_oc2refc signal is used as trigger output (tim_trgo2)
 *   0x6  Compare - tim_oc3refc signal is used as trigger output (tim_trgo2)
 *   0x7  Compare - tim_oc4refc signal is used as trigger output (tim_trgo2)
 *   0x8  Compare - tim_oc5refc signal is used as trigger output (tim_trgo2)
 *   0x9  Compare - tim_oc6refc signal is used as trigger output (tim_trgo2)
 *   0xA  Compare Pulse - tim_oc4refc rising or falling edges generate pulses on tim_trgo2
 *   0xB  Compare pulse - tim_oc6refc rising or falling edges generate pulses on tim_trgo2
 *   0xC  Compare pulse - tim_oc4refc or tim_oc6refc rising edges generate pulses on tim_trgo2
 *   0xD  Compare pulse - tim_oc4refc rising or tim_oc6refc falling edges generate pulses on tim_trgo2
 *   0xE  Compare pulse - tim_oc5refc or tim_oc6refc rising edges generate pulses on tim_trgo2
 *   0xF  Compare pulse - tim_oc5refc rising or tim_oc6refc falling edges generate pulses on tim_trgo2
 */
